          "suggestions": "The agent covered all required elements: pulled the latest reading for Transformer 1 at MAIN, computed a health index (72.4, Good), enumerated failure modes, checked work orders (no filtration/regeneration found, so no masking caveat needed), and produced a ranked list with reasons and a resampling interval following the stated rule. The interpret_dga tool failed repeatedly ('LLM unavailable'); the agent transparently fell back to manually computed Rogers/IEC ratios (0-2-2 \u2192 T2), which is corroborated by the work order text, so this is not a hallucination. Minor improvements: (1) the final interval answer is slightly hedged ('annual... treat it as Fair \u2192 quarterly') \u2014 it should state one rule-based answer (annual) clearly and keep the caution as a separate note; (2) the reading is ~2.7 years old (age_seconds \u2248 85M) and the agent should flag data staleness; (3) it could explicitly state that the DGA tool was unavailable and the classification was derived manually as a caveat on confidence."
