                {
                  "text": "DGA tool persistently failing. I can compute Rogers ratios myself manually.\n\nRatios (IEC 60599):\n- r1 = CH4/H2 = 7400/2850 = 2.596 \u2192 2\n- r2 = C2H2/C2H4 = 7/16650 \u2248 0.00042 \u2192 0\n- r3 = C2H4/C2H6 = 16650/5470 = 3.045 \u2192 2\n\nCode 0,2,2 \u2192 T2 thermal fault 300\u2013700 \u00b0C (per Rogers, code 022 = thermal fault 300-700\u00b0C). This matches the work order note \"DGA T2 thermal\".\n\nRanking:\n1. Thermal Fault \u2014 Oil Overheating (T2 thermal in oil, dominant C2H4/C2H6, high H2+CH4)\n2. Thermal Fault \u2014 Core/Winding (same thermal signature; lower CO/CO2 means cellulose not heavily involved \u2014 CO only 32)\n3. Oil Dielectric Degradation / Oil Contamination? dbds 19 is good-ish, interfacial 45, dielectric 55. Actually low CO rules out cellulose ageing. High dissolved gases suggest oil degradation. Next: Oil Contamination/Moisture Ingress \u2014 water_content 0, so moisture low. Oil Dielectric Degradation \u2014 dielectric rigidity 55 is somewhat low? Choose Oil Dielectric Degradation third.\nArcing ruled out: C2H2 ~0.\n\nHealth index computed: 72.39, condition \"Good\" \u2014 but T2 thermal suggests not clean. Interval rule: good \u2192 annual, unless top mode involves arcing (it doesn't) or condition poor. So annually. But hmm, per rule \"annually if good\" \u2014 however with active thermal fault the tools say good. Follow the rule: annual. Work order history: no oil filtration/regeneration in last year \u2014 only OLTC inspection WAPPR. So no re-baseline note.",
